 143:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h ****  * Target specific definitions and description of CAN message reception
 144:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h ****  *
 145:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h ****  * CAN messages in CANopenNode are usually received by its own thread or higher priority interrupt.
 146:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h ****  * messages are first filtered by hardware or by software. Thread then examines its 11-bit CAN-id a
 147:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h ****  * determines, to which \ref CO_obj "CANopenNode Object" it belongs to. After that it calls predefi
 148:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h ****  * function, which quickly pre-processes the message and fetches the relevant data. CANrx_callback(
 149:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h ****  * by each \ref CO_obj "CANopenNode Object" separately. Pre-processed fetched data are later proces
 150:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h ****  * thread.
 151:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h ****  *
 152:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h ****  * If \ref CO_obj "CANopenNode Object" reception of specific CAN message, it must first configure i
 153:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h ****  * object with the CO_CANrxBufferInit() function.
 154:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h ****  */
 155:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h **** 
 156:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h **** /**
 157:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h ****  * CAN receive callback function which pre-processes received CAN message
 158:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h ****  *
 159:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h ****  * It is called by fast CAN receive thread. Each \ref CO_obj "CANopenNode Object" defines its own a
 160:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h ****  * CO_CANrxBufferInit(), by passing function pointer.
 161:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h ****  *
 162:CANopen/301/CO_driver.h ****  * @param object pointer to specific \ref CO_obj "CANopenNode Object", registered with CO_CANrxBuff
